rp.zip)\n\nYes a warning does show (good!), but _why_ is there a warning, _why_ is the mesh invalid for this specific subdivision and this specific length? (shrinking the box mesh slightly fixes it)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6173192227/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6176178519","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124210#issuecomment-6176178519","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124210","id":6176178519,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcCEBVw","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T19:08:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:08:18Z","body":"Historically, CSG was defined to be always manifold, but in the past because of implementation quality CSG accepted any mesh.\n\nI switched Godot Engine to Manifold CSG because it promised that a manifold mesh will stay manifold, which means that a resulting non manifold mesh, calculated from a non-manifold mesh will stay non-manifold. We make non-manifold empty mesh. The benefit is that 10-20 mesh csg corruption bugs were fixed.\n\nMany of the mesh operators for Godot Engine CSG have been tuned to be manifold due to contributor effort, but if you go outside the precision the mesh operators tend to fail.\n\nI'm not sure how to resolve this.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6176178519/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]